    "Outer server API routes use the discovered major (16 in reviewed source); internal Player API remains v6.",
    "TFTP latest alias uses the current discovered API route, as attested by the v16 request example.",
    "Formal POST methods win over conflicting call batch GET examples; no alternate-method retries.",
    "Formal upnpav path wins over copy/pasted upnpigd examples.",
    "Voicemail country_code, VPN connection local_ip and recording IDs preserve declared/example scalar kinds.",
    "VPN IPSec authentication modes preserve dictionary/array shape and named dictionary keys.",
    "PVR record_time preserves integer/typed nested dictionary shape.",
    "PVR configuration update reads common success only because no result schema is provided."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "API signatures are covered, but this does not claim full field/schema coverage; omitted fields and unsupported variants are listed.",
    "Only the documented openvpn_routed server configuration PUT is exposed; no speculative generic server configuration PUT or VPN start/stop routes.",
    "Timestamp wire values remain integers; no universal unit or epoch is assumed.",
    "No implicit retry is introduced, including side-effecting VPN configuration downloads.",
    "Read/write projections omit marked read-only and example-only fields from writes; unset values are omitted, false and zero are explicit, unproven explicit null is rejected.",
    "Open-ended author-defined Player foreground context alone uses JsonElement as documented.",
    "No source generator project was necessary; built-in System.Text.Json generated metadata covers the closed contracts."
